<title>USA: Westinghouse sees job cuts at energy unit.</title>
<headline>Westinghouse sees job cuts at energy unit.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Westinghouse Electric Corp Chairman Michael Jordan on Wednesday said staff reductions in the company's Energy Systems unit were possible this year.</p>
<p>&quot;Energy Systems is going to be a leaner business going forward,&quot; he told reporters at media briefing after the company's annual meeting in Minneapolis.</p>
<p>When asked if that would entail staff reductions, Jordan said, &quot;Yes, we think so. Their revenues have been declining and that will impact staffing.&quot;</p>
<p>Jordan declined to comment on how many jobs may be eliminated.</p>
</text>
